# Observed oracle for PA-08-F70 / inc-tek.8.8: the flame tongue sword's
# tongue-of-flame lash must be able to yank a LARGE corporeal creature.
#
# THE PROMISE. The sword's own page (lib/m_items.irh, the "flame tongue"
# entity) says the lash acts "if the victim still lives and is a Large or
# smaller corporeal creature". So a Large victim is inside the rule.
#
# THE DEFECT. The lash effect ("tongue of flame" EA_BLAST) gated the
# opposed-Strength yank on `if (EVictim->GetAttr(A_SIZ) >= SZ_LARGE) return
# NOTHING;` -- an off-by-one that bailed for Large AND larger, so only
# Medium-and-smaller ever reached the contest. Brian ruled prose wins: include
# Large, exclude only LARGER. The gate must read `> SZ_LARGE`.
#
# WHAT IS OBSERVED. One session hits a summoned otyugh with the activated
# lash. The otyugh is Large (lib/mon1.irh: Size SZ_LARGE), corporeal (a MA_BEAST
# with no M_INCOR) and weak-armed (Str 11, modifier 0), so a barbarian wins the
# opposed Strength test and the yank fires.
#
#   ON A BUILD WITHOUT THE FIX (gate `>= SZ_LARGE`): the ray deals its 4d8 and
#   then falls silent -- the size gate returns before the contest, so NO
#   "tongue of flame lashes around ... pulls <him> to your side" line and no
#   "holds ground" line ever prints.
#   ON A BUILD WITH THE FIX (gate `> SZ_LARGE`): the same otyugh is now inside
#   the rule, the barbarian wins the Strength test and the lash prints
#   "Your tongue of flame lashes around the otyugh and pulls it to your side."
#
# WHY AN OTYUGH. It must be Large, corporeal, survive the 4d8 ray, and have a
# low enough Strength that the wielder wins the opposed test on this seed. The
# otyugh's Str 11 (modifier 0) against the barbarian's positive modifier makes
# the win reliable, and its 6 Hit Dice leave it standing after 4d8.
#
# WHY THE MONSTERS ARE FROZEN. The otyugh stands one square east while the
# sword is readied and activated. An unfrozen otyugh (Rend, natural grab) would
# maul a first level barbarian first. Freeze Monsters leaves it in the world but
# denies it its turns.
#
# Menu letters move when a list changes. Run with the seed the check supplies.

@include chargen.keys

# --- WIZARD SWITCHES: Auto-Identify (so the sword's activation is named) and
# --- Freeze Monsters. Row 1 is Auto-Identify, row 10 is Freeze Monsters.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN
SPACE                   # Auto-Identify Items
DOWN*9
SPACE                   # Freeze Monsters
ESC

# --- PUT A FLAME TONGUE IN THE CHARACTER'S HAND -----------------------------
# RIGHT*10 walks the glyph row to Specific Weapons. The candidate list shows
# three rows with the MIDDLE one selected, so the walk stops on the pass where
# the row BELOW the wanted one -- "Javelin of Lightning", the AI_WEAPON entity
# that follows "flame tongue" in lib/m_items.irh -- first appears.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10
@until "Javelin of Lightning" DOWN
ENTER
2                       # "Enter Item Level:" -- the sword's own INITIAL_PLUS
ENTER
b                       # Weapon Hand; the slot lettering skips 'd', the Drop key
SPACE                   # swap the sword into it
n                       # decline wielding a long sword two-handed
s                       # stow the orcish knife the swap pushed into the air
@dump:wielded
ESC

# --- SUMMON THE OTYUGH THREE SQUARES EAST -----------------------------------
# Three squares away, not adjacent, so a successful yank has somewhere to pull
# the otyugh FROM: the lash lands it "directly at his feet", one square east,
# and the map glyph moves from three east to one east. The ray's range is
# 3 + max(0, Charisma modifier) squares = 5 here (Charisma 14), so three
# squares is well inside it.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Beast"
@choose "otyugh"
RIGHT*3                 # the location cursor starts on the player; three east
ENTER
@dump:summoned

# --- ACTIVATE THE TONGUE OF FLAME AND TARGET THE OTYUGH ---------------------
# 'a' opens the activation menu; the sword is its only activatable item, listed
# as menu entry [a] (the @dump:activate-menu screen shows "Long Sword, Flame
# Tongue +2", which the check reads back before trusting anything). The second
# 'a' selects it.
#
# Two target prompts follow. The activation handler prompts first ("Select a
# target:"); RIGHT enters the target ring at the nearest creature east -- the
# adjacent otyugh -- and ENTER confirms it. The handler then RedirectEff's to
# the "tongue of flame" blast, which raises its own prompt ("Choose your
# target:"); RIGHT and ENTER pick the otyugh again. The ray then deals 4d8 and
# runs the opposed-Strength yank.
a
@dump:activate-menu
a
RIGHT
ENTER
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:lash

# --- READ THE OTYUGH BACK ---------------------------------------------------
# The yank is silent to a scrollback that only keeps two lines, so the oracle
# reads the otyugh's own wizard-mode Dump instead. A yank knocks its victim
# down (GainPermStati(PRONE) in the lash), and a frozen otyugh never stands, so
# PRONE persists in the dump's Stati list. On a build WITHOUT the fix the size
# gate returns before the knockdown and the Stati list carries no Prone; on a
# build WITH it, Prone is present. The dump's HP line also proves the 4d8 ray
# left the otyugh alive, so the yank had a living Large victim to act on.
w
@choose "Examine Nearby Things"
@until "otyugh (class" RIGHT
@dump:otyugh-after
ESC

@quit
